  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="b552-a81c-753b-6d75" name="Trojan War (Chariot Wars) - List Notes" publicationId="513c-2d0a-024a-da5a" hidden="false">
      <description>TROJAN WAR ARMY LIST (Chariot Wars, pp.41-46): Mycenaean, Minoan &amp; Trojan armies, 1600 BC to 800 BC.
Characters up to 25%; at least one character to command. A small army of 1,000 points can be commanded by a Senior Officer (Hero) rather than a General (King or Lawageta). Chariotry up to HALF the points value. Infantry at least 25%. Allies &amp; Mercenaries up to HALF.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS:
[Trojan War]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Chariotry: up to 50%
  Infantry: at least 25%
  Allies &amp; Mercenaries: up to 50%
  Standard composition.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
